    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_6420d1a1",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: chuck_norris_meme; hasOverallIntent: misogynous; overall-intent-description: The image shows an elderly man in military gear, with text that reads 'chuck norris?' and 'never heard of her.' The joke relies on the gendered misrepresentation of Chuck Norris, a male action star, by implying he is a woman ('her') whom the speaker has never heard of. This is a form of misogynous humor because it uses the stereotype that women are unfamiliar or unknown to the speaker, and it mocks the idea of a male figure being mistaken for a female one, which can be seen as reinforcing gendered assumptions and objectifying women by reducing them to a 'never heard of' status. The meme's intent is to create humor through this gendered misrepresentation, which can be interpreted as misogynous due to its reliance on gender stereotypes and the implication that women are less known or less significant than men.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_b00fca7c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
